>>>Now that everyone is finished with dogs, here's another query: 3.0 is going
>>>to have more different monsters, including succubi and incubi.  What should
>>>they do?

Here are a couple of suggestions for 3.0:

When you have a polymorph control ring and are asked what to turn into
you should only be able to turn into something that you have already
encountered. e.g. you have already killed one so have had time to examine
it, or you were randomly polymorphed into one. The healer would be the
exception, being able to change into things not already encountered (much
as the wizard has a chance of being able to write an unknown spell on a
blank scroll). If you have already seen one but not killed one yet then
you might have a chance of being able to polymorph into one (say 50/50),
or if a wisdom stat. has been added it might then depend on your wisdom.

Another more tentative suggestion is changing the dungeon floorplan
size to fit the window. Perhaps I should elaborate further. I use an
xterm to play nethack and would like to see all of the window used if
I can get one larger than 80x24. I tried just tweaking the ROWS and COLS,
and MAXNROFROOM (or whatever it is) but the program core dumped when I
ran it. What would be nice is to have nethack check the size of my window
and scale the floorplan size to it. This might prove difficult for bones
files since the sizes would be different. However then the idea could be
expanded a little to make things possibly more realistic. Each time a
level is made give it a random size within the bounds of the window that
is being used, with a minimum area of 22x80, so that a normal terminal
screen will be full, but a larger window may have different sizes of
level. When a bones file is read in if it will not fit in the current window
mark it as unused and just make a normal level.

